                <pb facs="1191" n="1033" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1033"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé Wilson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Boot directs the embassy to inquire if Japanese Government would acquiesce
                    in the American representative at Seoul being styled agent and consul-general,
                    thus following a usual precedent in the case of protected countries and
                    facilitating business relations with the Japanese resident.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
